Hi Learnosity Support,

We've been seeing sporadic client errors since August with the Assess API. We're on v2024.2.lts.  The error shows up as a "RangeError Maximum call stack size exceeded" on the client inside Learnosity code.  It happens to a small percentage of students.  

We've finally traced it down.  We have essentially this code:

handler = (time) => {
  if (expired(time)) {
    itemsApp.off('time:change', handler);
    handleExpired();
  }
}
itemsApp.on('time:change', handler);

This used to work fine before August, but now occasionally the off() call will itself trigger the time:change event and recurse into the handler again.  This leads to infinite recursion.  I was able to reproduce this by stepping into the off function a few levels and then letting the code continue.  Every time the browser would trigger an exception.

We have a workaround to ensure the off() can't be called twice, but I think there's probably a bug here.  I wouldn't expect the time:change event to trigger from inside itself like this.  I'll attach a stack trace.

Thanks,
-matt

